<title>SPAIN: Spanish unemployment fell 27,000 in August.</title>
<headline>Spanish unemployment fell 27,000 in August.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish unemployment fell 27,000 in August, according to advance data released by the Employment Ministry.</p>
<p>This would bring the total number of unemployed down to 2.14 million for a jobless rate of 13.5 percent, based on July figures. Unemployment stood at 13.67 percent in July.</p>
<p>The full August data were originally scheduled for release next week.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2161</p>
